      "Responses mix a routing record with narrative, such as \"Here is the record: {...} Let me know if you need anything else.\" The consumer extracts the first {...} with a regular expression, and 1.8% of responses fail on nested braces or stray text. The service runs on Claude Sonnet 5.5. Which change protects downstream routing?",
